From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FerrionOS <noreply@ferrionos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:07:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] layout: Cascade new windows of a free workspace (F5)

The first window of a free workspace opens centered, as niri already
places a floating window. Each next window without a place of its own
opens 32 pixels, the height of a title strip, lower and to the right of
the window on top, and at the top left of the working area when it
would leave it there. A window with a stored place, a
`default-floating-position` rule, a parent it opens next to, or a
fullscreen or maximized state keeps niri's placement, and so does every
window on a columns workspace.

The placement is made where F4 already sends a free workspace's new
windows to the floating layout, so floating.rs is not changed.

Agent-written tests and their test-only helpers were removed under ADR 0025.
The source commit in the header records the original patch provenance;
this patch is regenerated against the preceding test-free stage. Upstream
tests remain, with the config snapshots adapted to the production fields.
